#
# NuPhy Air75 V2 WebHID/VIA Access Rule
#
# Vendor ID:  19f5
# Product ID: 3246
#
# TECHNICAL NOTE ON UACCESS AND FILE NUMBERING:
# Systemd processes udev rules in strict lexical (alphabetical/numerical) order.
# The rule responsible for evaluating TAG+="uaccess" and applying dynamic POSIX ACLs
# for the active logged-in graphical user is /lib/udev/rules.d/73-seat-late.rules.
#
# Rules with a prefix higher than 73 (e.g., 99-nuphy.rules) set TAG+="uaccess" too late,
# causing systemd-logind to skip setting user ACLs on the device node. Using a prefix
# below 73 (such as 70-nuphy.rules) ensures the node is tagged before seat evaluation.
#
# SEAT ATTRIBUTION & PATH ID:
# Kernel hidraw interfaces often lack seat attribution data by default. Importing systemd's
# "path_id" builtin forces physical path resolution, and explicitly setting ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat0"
# guarantees systemd-logind binds the node to the active desktop session to grant dynamic ACLs.

KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="19f5", ATTRS{idProduct}=="3246", IMPORT{builtin}="path_id", ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat0", TAG+="uaccess"
